<Layout title="Terms & Conditions | Luxury Modules" description="The terms on which you may use the Luxury Modules website, including how our pricing, imagery and reservation process should be understood.">
<div class="pagehero">
  <p class="kicker">Legal</p>
  <h1>Website Terms &amp; Conditions</h1>
  <p>The basis on which you use this site, and how to read what is on it.</p>
  <p style="font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);margin-top:10px">Last updated: {updated}</p>
</div>

<section><div class="wrap" style="max-width:820px">

  <h2>Who you are dealing with</h2><div class="gold-rule"></div>
  <p>This site is operated by Luxury Modules Limited, registered in England and Wales, company number 16007852, registered office 111-113 High Street, Evesham, Worcestershire, WR11 4XP. Contact: <a href="mailto:sales@luxurymodules.co.uk">sales@luxurymodules.co.uk</a>.</p>
  <p>By using this site you accept these terms. If you do not accept them, please do not use the site.</p>

  <h2 style="margin-top:44px">Pricing on this site</h2><div class="gold-rule"></div>
  <p>All prices shown are indicative "from" prices, exclude VAT, and were last reviewed in January 2026. They are not an offer and do not form a contract.</p>
  <p>Groundworks, access, site conditions, planning requirements and specification all affect the final figure, which is why a firm price follows a scoping call and site assessment rather than a web page. The guide bands shown in the module configurator are estimates on the same basis.</p>

  <h2 style="margin-top:44px">The reservation fee</h2><div class="gold-rule"></div>
  <p>Submitting a specification through the configurator is a request, not a purchase. Nothing is charged through this website. If you ask us to proceed, we will contact you to confirm the specification and issue an invoice for the reservation fee separately, and the terms of that reservation will be set out at that point.</p>

  <h2 style="margin-top:44px">Imagery and specifications</h2><div class="gold-rule"></div>
  <p>Photographs, renders and concept images on this site illustrate the range and the design language. They may show configurations, finishes, landscaping or locations that are not included in a standard specification, and some are concept renders rather than photographs of completed UK projects. What is included in your project is what appears in your written specification.</p>
  <p>Dimensions, timescales and performance figures are typical rather than guaranteed, and are confirmed project by project.</p>

  <h2 style="margin-top:44px">Planning and consents</h2><div class="gold-rule"></div>
  <p>Guidance on this site about planning permission and permitted development is general information, not advice on your property. Planning outcomes depend on your site, your local authority and the details of your proposal. Where we manage a planning application for you, we will say so in writing, but we cannot guarantee a particular decision.</p>

  <h2 style="margin-top:44px">Our content</h2><div class="gold-rule"></div>
  <p>The content of this site, including text, imagery, layout and design, is owned by Luxury Modules Limited or used with permission from our manufacturing partner. You may view and print pages for your own use in considering a project. You may not republish or use our content commercially without our written permission.</p>
  <p>Revonia is the trade mark of its owner and is used here to describe our partnership.</p>

  <h2 style="margin-top:44px">Liability</h2><div class="gold-rule"></div>
  <p>We take reasonable care to keep this site accurate and available, but we do not guarantee that it is error-free or uninterrupted. To the extent permitted by law, we are not liable for loss arising from reliance on general information published here, as distinct from a written specification, quotation or contract we have issued to you.</p>
  <p>Nothing in these terms limits our liability for death or personal injury caused by negligence, for fraud, or for anything else that cannot lawfully be limited. If you are a consumer, these terms do not affect your statutory rights.</p>

  <h2 style="margin-top:44px">Governing law</h2><div class="gold-rule"></div>
  <p>These terms are governed by the law of England and Wales, and the courts of England and Wales have jurisdiction.</p>

  <div style="margin-top:40px"><a class="btn" href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> <a class="btn ghost" href="/cookies/" style="margin-left:8px">Cookie Policy</a></div>
